# Every text file is checked out with LF, Windows included. Git for Windows
# sets `core.autocrlf`, which would otherwise hand a checkout there CRLF:
# the tests read their fixtures and goldens as bytes (`include_str!`, a
# marker written byte for byte, a block rendered in the file's own line
# endings), and what the CLI prints ends its lines with `\n` on every
# platform, so a fixture is the same bytes everywhere or the suite
# disagrees with itself. `auto` leaves a binary file, an image, as it is.
* text=auto eol=lf
